<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ras al-Khaimah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras">Ras</a> al-Khaimah is a port city on the northern coast of the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a> and capital of the emirate of the same name. It became the main base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Al Qasimi</a> in the 18th century and was attacked by British expeditions in 1809 and 1819. The emirate joined the United Arab Emirates in February 1972, two months after its foundation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ras-al-khaimah.jpg" alt="Ras al-Khaimah" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stevenmccombe · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_RAK_City_from_Al_Qawasim_Corniche_flagpole.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
